#. type: TH
#: unity.1:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "unity"
msgstr "aferdis"

#. type: TH
#: unity.1:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "9 December 2010"
msgstr "9 deg dujambeṛ 2010"

#. type: TH
#: unity.1:1 unity-panel-service.1:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Linux User's Manual"
msgstr "Adlis n useqdac n Linux"

#. type: SH
#: unity.1:3 unity-panel-service.1:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr "ISEM"

#. type: Plain text
#: unity.1:5
msgid "unity - wrapper for starting the unity shell and handling fallback"
msgstr ""
"aferdis - taneɣrit tasdurayant i usenker n shell n uferdis d usesfer aneggaru"

#. type: SH
#: unity.1:6 unity-panel-service.1:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr "SYNOPSIS"

#. type: Plain text
#: unity.1:9
msgid "B<unity> [I<options>]"
msgstr "B<unity> [I<options>]"

#. type: SH
#: unity.1:11 unity-panel-service.1:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "AGLAM"

#. type: Plain text
#: unity.1:13
msgid ""
"The B<unity> program can be used to start the Unity shell as a compiz "
"module, and to specify how to handle logging, debugging, as well as how to "
"deal with the user's profile."
msgstr ""
"Ahil B<unity> yezmer ad yettuseqdac i usenker n shell Unity am uzegrir "
"amagnu, i ufran n wamek ara tesferkeḍ taɣamsa, tamseɣtayt akked wamek daɣen "
"ara tesneqdeḍ amaɣnu n useqdac."

#. type: SH
#: unity.1:14 unity-panel-service.1:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr "IΓEWWAREN"

#. type: IP
#: unity.1:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--advanced-debug>"
msgstr "B<--advanced-debug>"

#. type: Plain text
#: unity.1:17
msgid ""
"Runs unity under debugging (using GDB or another debugger tool) to help "
"tracking issues. Should only be used on request from a developper following "
"a bug report."
msgstr ""
"Isselkam unity ddaw n temseɣtayt ( suseqdec n GDB neɣ afecku-nniḍen n "
"umseɣti) i uɛiwen deg uḍfar n wuguren. Ilaq ad tettuseqdac kan mi ara tt-id-"
"isuter uneflay ssebba n uneqqis n wabug."

#. type: IP
#: unity.1:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--log>\\ I<filename>"
msgstr "B<--log>\\ I<filename>"

#. type: Plain text
#: unity.1:20
msgid ""
"This parameter, followed by a path or filename, tells the Unity shell to "
"store logs in the specified file."
msgstr ""
"Aɣewwar-a, yettwaḍefren s ubrid, neɣ s yisem n ufaylu, yeqqar i shell Unity "
"ad tekles iɣmisen deg ufaylu yettwafernen."

#. type: IP
#: unity.1:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--reset>"
msgstr "B<--reset>"

#. type: Plain text
#: unity.1:23
msgid ""
"This option allows the user to reset profile parameters in compiz and "
"restart the Unity shell with default settings."
msgstr ""
"Taxtiṛt tessirig aseqdac ad iwennez iɣewwaren n umaɣnu deg compiz akked ad "
"yales asenker n shell Unity s yiɣewwaren imezwer."

#. type: IP
#: unity.1:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--verbose>"
msgstr "B<--verbose>"

#. type: Plain text
#: unity.1:26
msgid ""
"This option turns on displaying additional debugging output for the Unity "
"shell. It can be used by the user to debug configuration issues. This option "
"is often used along with the B<--log> option to save output to a file."
msgstr ""
"Taxtiṛt-a tutturmad i uskan n tuffɣa n temseɣtayt-nniḍen i shell Unity. "
"Tezmer ad tettuseqdac sɣur asegdac i useɣti n wuguren n twila. Taxtiṛt-a "
"tezga tettuseqdac akked textiṛt B<--log> i usekles n tuffɣa deg ufaylu."

#. type: SH
#: unity.1:27 unity-panel-service.1:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "SEE ALSO"
msgstr "WALI DAΓEN"

#. type: Plain text
#: unity.1:29
msgid "B<unity-panel-service> (1)"
msgstr "B<unity-panel-service> (1)"

#. type: TH
#: unity-panel-service.1:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "unity-panel-service"
msgstr "aferdis-agalis-tanfa"

#. type: TH
#: unity-panel-service.1:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "8 December 2010"
msgstr "8 deg dujambeṛ 2010"

#. type: Plain text
#: unity-panel-service.1:5
msgid ""
"unity-panel-service - program for drawing the panel with the unity shell."
msgstr "aferdis-agalis-tanfa - ahil i usuneɣ n ugalis akked uferdis shell."

#. type: Plain text
#: unity-panel-service.1:8
msgid "B<unity-panel-service>"
msgstr "B<unity-panel-service>"

#. type: Plain text
#: unity-panel-service.1:12
msgid ""
"The B<unity-panel-service> program is normally started automatically by the "
"Unity shell (which gets started as a compiz module) and is used to draw "
"panels which can then be used for the global menu, or to hold indicators."
msgstr ""
"Ahil B<unity-panel-service> yettusenker s wudem awurman s shell Unity (i "
"yettusnekren am uzegrir compiz) syen yettuseqdac i usuneɣ n yigalisen i "
"izemren ad ttusqedcen i wumuɣ amatu, neɣ tuttfa n yinamalen."

#. type: Plain text
#: unity-panel-service.1:15
msgid "B<unity-panel-service> takes no options."
msgstr "B<unity-panel-service> ur yettawi ara iɣewwaren."

#. type: SH
#: unity-panel-service.1:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "NOTES"
msgstr "TIZMILIN"
